#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128893 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129079 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "da47f01b-0db0-586f-9d55-5bd4c952afb6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Tangent to Plane a Level Surface"}] :question/id #uuid "09499f38-a497-5f59-9cb2-0882a5853320" :question/math-academy-id "e-3368" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y,z) = x^2+y^2+z^2,$ find the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(2,-2,1).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z) = k$ at the point $(x_0,y_0,z_0)$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\nabla \\! f(x_0,y_0,z_0) \\cdot \\langle x-x_0, \\: y-y_0, \\: z-z_0 \\rangle  = 0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $(x_0,y_0,z_0) =(2,-2,1)\\mathbin{:}$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}\\,i+{f}_{y}\\,j+{f}_{z}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})\\text{ }k \\\\  & =2x\\text{ }i+2y\\text{ }j+2z\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇\\,f(2,-2,1) & =2(2)\\text{ }i+2(-2)\\text{ }j+2(1)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =4\\,i-4\\,j+2\\text{ }k \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,-4\\,,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇\\,f(2,-2,1)\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y-(-2),\\,z-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨4,\\,-4,\\,2⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y+2,\\,z-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ 4(x-2)-4(y+2)+2(z-1) & =0 \\\\ 4x-4y+2z-18 & =0 \\\\ 2x-2y+z-9 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128998 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129179 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "16f4bd05-1f30-576c-a538-a0ac4d533b7a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Tangent Plane of a Surface Given Implicitly Using the Gradient Vector"}] :question/id #uuid "9091e2dc-5b05-5ae7-a498-9de0483ec375" :question/math-academy-id "e-6183" :question/problem "Consider the surface $z^3y^2 =x^2-5.$ Find the equation of the tangent plane to this surface at the point $(-1,2,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{3}{y}^{2} & ={x}^{2}-5 \\\\ {z}^{3}{y}^{2}-{x}^{2} & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y,z) = z^3y^2 - x^2,$ our surface can be viewed as the level surface $f(x,y,z)=-5.$ \n\nRecall that the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z) = k$ at the point $(x_0,y_0,z_0)$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\nabla f(x_0,y_0,z_0) \\cdot \\langle x-x_0, \\: y-y_0, \\: z-z_0 \\rangle  = 0.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $(-1,2,-1)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({z}^{3}{y}^{2}-{x}^{2})\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({z}^{3}{y}^{2}-{x}^{2})\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({z}^{3}{y}^{2}-{x}^{2})\\text{ }k \\\\  & =(-2x)\\text{ }i+2{z}^{3}y\\text{ }j+3{z}^{2}{y}^{2}\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇\\,f(-1,2,-1) & =(-2)(-1)\\text{ }i+2(-1)^{3}(2)\\text{ }j+3(-1)^{2}(2)^{2}\\text{ }k \\\\  & =2\\,i-4j+12\\,k \\\\  & =⟨2,-4,12⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(-1,2,-1)\\cdot ⟨x-(-1),\\,y-2,\\,z-(-1)⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨2,-4,12⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y-2,\\,z+1⟩ & =0 \\\\ 2(x+1)-4(y-2)+12(z+1) & =0 \\\\ 2x-4y+12z+22 & =0 \\\\ x-2y+6z+11 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368502 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129179 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "16f4bd05-1f30-576c-a538-a0ac4d533b7a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Tangent Plane of a Surface Given Implicitly Using the Gradient Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f31566f3-5a9f-50b0-8133-875da6050b2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+y+4z+3=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368504} {:answer/id #uuid "0a4508b7-d6bf-54c2-9c11-8ec5041ce685" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4z-x-y-5=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368505} {:answer/id #uuid "30c0d468-01b5-599b-87fa-e43055e8e8d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+y+4z-3=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368506} {:answer/id #uuid "c0d82b5d-43cc-5e7b-be7a-81f6c28fddb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x+4y+z-3=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368507} {:answer/id #uuid "37714307-6eae-52a9-ace4-a33d77834680" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x+4y+z+3=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368508}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30c0d468-01b5-599b-87fa-e43055e8e8d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+y+4z-3=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368506} :answer-field/id #uuid "4631e236-0c05-57c6-a8a7-da1ff59269c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368503}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2fd20ce6-a0d3-5928-9428-ede66532d00e" :question/math-academy-id "q-37594" :question/problem "Consider the surface $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y+2{z}^{2})=1-x.$ Find the equation of the tangent plane to that surface at the point $(1,-2,1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y+2{z}^{2}) & =1-x \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(y+2{z}^{2})+x-1 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nIf we set $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y+2{z}^{2})+x-1$, our surface can be viewed as the level surface $f(x,y,z)=0.$\n\nRecall that the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $(1,-2,1):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y+2{z}^{2})+x-1\\,)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y+2{z}^{2})+x-1\\,)\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(y+2{z}^{2})+x-1\\,)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =\\text{ }i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(y+2{z}^{2})\\text{ }j+4z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(y+2{z}^{2})\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇\\,f(1,-2,1) & =\\text{ }i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡((-2)+2(1)^{2})\\text{ }j+4(1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡((-2)+2(1)^{2})\\text{ }k \\\\  & =i+j+4\\,k \\\\  & =⟨1,1,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(1,-2,1)\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y+2,\\,z-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨1,1,4⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,\\,y+2,\\,z-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ (x-1)+(y+2)+4(z-1) & =0 \\\\ x+y+4z-3 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348448 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129079 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "da47f01b-0db0-586f-9d55-5bd4c952afb6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Tangent to Plane a Level Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1663e019-c7d9-5e2d-9dbe-71ebddf8290b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+2y+7z-36=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345549} {:answer/id #uuid "6571ddc7-83ee-51ae-b69b-3a73f8b9bf0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8x+y+z-23=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346236} {:answer/id #uuid "925d13bb-c92d-5f35-b0f3-4234c87d30e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8x+2y+5z+7=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346631} {:answer/id #uuid "c6840705-8e54-503e-be26-3574f6f8d412" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+y+z-9=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347078} {:answer/id #uuid "e082281f-2341-5fb5-83fb-0ba87ed7944d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+2y+5z-28=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347320}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e082281f-2341-5fb5-83fb-0ba87ed7944d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+2y+5z-28=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347320} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9a7661b-5846-57e9-be3c-6d40db58cd30" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347954}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bbcded61-18ec-5362-9f48-c67e58a60e0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-80767" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y,z)=xy-yz-xz$, find the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface that passes  through the point where $(x,y,z)=(2,3,4).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(2,3,4):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy-yz-xz)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy-yz-xz)\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xy-yz-xz)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =(y-z)\\text{ }i+(x-z)\\text{ }j+(-y-x)k \\\\ ∇\\,f(2,3,4) & =(3-4)\\text{ }i+(2-4)\\text{ }j+(-3-2)k \\\\  & =-1\\text{ }i-2\\text{ }j-5k \\\\  & =⟨-1,-2,-5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(2,3,4)\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y-3,\\,z-4⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨-1,-2,-5⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y-3,\\,z-4⟩ & =0 \\\\ -(x-2)-2(y-3)-5(z-4) & =0 \\\\ -x-2y-5z+28 & =0 \\\\ x+2y+5z-28 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348449 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129079 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "da47f01b-0db0-586f-9d55-5bd4c952afb6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Tangent to Plane a Level Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34d6c237-b645-5134-bed0-3db87cd111a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+8y+4z-14=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345809} {:answer/id #uuid "5451ea98-cec6-5c7d-adef-f96ea6bd234c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+4y+4z-10=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346066} {:answer/id #uuid "8e60e7e0-b0eb-5453-8a9e-93ecd04c25ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+8y+z-13=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346590} {:answer/id #uuid "cfc13077-10ec-5459-801a-f68bf9ba6620" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+2y+z-5=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347169} {:answer/id #uuid "f41a2ef9-7eb7-5e8a-8edf-fd77bb60489a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+y+z-6=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347514}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cfc13077-10ec-5459-801a-f68bf9ba6620" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+2y+z-5=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347169} :answer-field/id #uuid "384d5f4d-e2ac-598f-9b2f-eabbb7bb39e6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347700}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4798bf87-b861-5528-ad8e-12b959ab1ff8" :question/math-academy-id "q-80769" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2}$,  find the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(2,1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇\\,f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(2,1,1):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2})\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2})\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2})\\text{ }k \\\\  & =2x\\text{ }i+8y\\text{ }j+4z\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇\\,f(2,1,1) & =2(2)\\text{ }i+8(1)j+4(1)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =4\\,i+8\\,j+4\\,k \\\\  & =⟨4,8,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇\\,f(2,1,1)\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y-1,\\,z-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨4,8,4⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y-1,\\,z-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ 4(x-2)+8(y-1)+4(z-1) & =0 \\\\ 4x+8y+4z-20 & =0 \\\\ x+2y+z-5 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368852 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129179 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "16f4bd05-1f30-576c-a538-a0ac4d533b7a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Tangent Plane of a Surface Given Implicitly Using the Gradient Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14878a31-11ea-5c7e-84d0-fd09663b9dec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11x-24y+z+62=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368854} {:answer/id #uuid "93faa97f-405e-5443-9dbd-03d61733af8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11x-4y-z+62=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368855} {:answer/id #uuid "b05712f5-94c2-5c99-92eb-789baeed8e32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-24y+z+26=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368856} {:answer/id #uuid "17bfc5b8-7e32-54b3-ac77-8535f2ab4942" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-42y+11z-26=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368857} {:answer/id #uuid "a8436930-5933-58e8-ba5e-4ae3f1d425c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11x+24y+z-62=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368858}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14878a31-11ea-5c7e-84d0-fd09663b9dec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11x-24y+z+62=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368854} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4bef21b-f7ad-5f9a-819c-86eb77bec1f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368853}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "57e1cfb5-fa24-5598-9daa-442855c8439f" :question/math-academy-id "q-86470" :question/problem "Consider the surface $z{x}^{4}+18=x+2{y}^{3}.$ Find the equation of the tangent plane to that surface at the point $(-1,2,-3).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z{x}^{4}+18 & =x+2{y}^{3} \\\\ z{x}^{4}-x-2{y}^{3} & =-18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y,z)=z{x}^{4}-x-2{y}^{3},$ our surface can be viewed as the level surface $f(x,y,z)=-18.$ \n\nRecall that the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $(-1,2,-3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(z{x}^{4}-x-2{y}^{3})\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(z{x}^{4}-x-2{y}^{3})\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(z{x}^{4}-x-2{y}^{3})\\text{ }k \\\\  & =(4{x}^{3}z-1)\\text{ }i-6{y}^{2}\\text{ }j+{x}^{4}\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇\\,f(-1,2,-3) & =(4(-1)^{3}(-3)-1)\\text{ }i-6(2)^{2}\\text{ }j+(-1)^{4}\\text{ }k \\\\  & =11\\,i-24j+k \\\\  & =⟨11,-24,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(-1,2,-3)\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y-2,\\,z+3⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨11,-24,1⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,\\,y-2,\\,z+3⟩ & =0 \\\\ 11(x+1)-24(y-2)+(z+3) & =0 \\\\ 11x-24y+z+62 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
